<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav April inflation 0.1 pct vs 1.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav April inflation 0.1 pct vs 1.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV INFLATION	  APRIL	MARCH     APRIL 1996</p>
<p> monthly RPI index rise    + 0.1	+ 1.0	 + 3.1</p>
<p> yr/yr percent change	+22.7	+26.4	+115.1</p>
<p>NOTES -- April RPI was 17.8 percent up against the average in 1996.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-April RPI was 17 percent up against the average in 1996 and 29.4 percent up against the same four-month period last year.</p>
<p>April RPI was up 3.1 percent on December last year.</p>
<p>Figures refer to the Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>-- Gordana Kukic, Belgrade Newsroom +381 11 222 4254</p>
